# Quest for Ancient Secrets: "your graveyard" is its controller's (CR 109.5), and the owner's does not matter. Bot1 casts
# Harmless Offering giving Bot2 control of Quest. Harmless Offering then lands in Bot1's graveyard, Quest's owner's, but Bot2
# controls Quest, so Bot1 is asked nothing (the refusal). On its turn Bot2 casts Thought Scour on Bot1: Bot1's two milled
# cards are in neither Bot2's graveyard nor the cards of its Quest, and the spell, put into Bot2's graveyard, gives Bot2 the
# trigger, accepted: one counter, on the Quest Bot2 controls.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Quest for Ancient Secrets
Harmless Offering
Thought Scour
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Thought Scour
Island x5
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Quest for Ancient Secrets.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Quest for Ancient Secrets)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
! Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Thought Scour.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Quest for Ancient Secrets.Counters.Quest = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Island; Island; Harmless Offering
Bot2.Graveyard = Thought Scour
